{"kind":"request","text":"Fix what the Mac mini validation of launchd supervision (V1) and HTTPS with a self-signed certificate (V4) found, and carry its results into the self-hosting kit. Hugh directed the validation on 2026-10-27, and the HTTPS approach: a self-signed certificate that the user trusts is the lightweight default; a user-supplied certificate and tunnel options are documented alternatives.\n\nSetup: Caddy 2.11.7, SeaweedFS 4.51 and celld v0.6.3 as LaunchDaemons running as user inguz on the Mac mini (macOS 27.2, FileVault on), with the room Worker of main 4419008a and the qualification entry of the SeaweedFS record (request 373596467cb3e30567a54987a277fb65cc2c37d6). Evidence: read-only folder ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-27-mac-launchd-https/ (133 files, SHA256SUMS; REPORT.md has every figure and how it was taken; WITHHELD.txt names the withheld keys and secrets).\n\nVerdict: no blocker in the platform. No acknowledged act was lost or duplicated across kill -9 and SIGTERM of each service, a cold start, KeepAlive with SeaweedFS down, and a macOS authenticated restart under 1 act/s load (1,100 acknowledged acts checked entry by entry; services up 25.8 s after boot with no one logged in). TLS, browser joins and acts, long idle streams, MCP over HTTPS and the proxy's ownership of CF-Connecting-IP all work through Caddy. Three findings block a usable local deployment, all in dap or celld:\n\n1. Live updates do not work on celld 0.6.3. `/v1/scopes/\u003cscope\u003e/stream` answers 200 and ends at once, direct and through Caddy; celld logs \"RPC streams cannot cross isolate boundaries yet\". The room page also has no live updates of its own: a second participant saw a new comment only after a reload. Decide whether dap serves the stream without an RPC stream across isolates, or waits for celld, and what the page does.\n2. Behind the proxy the Worker sees `http://` URLs. Hosted MCP agent creation is refused 403 (rule \"service\") because the service is taken from `url.origin`. The qualification entry used a test-only shim (rebuild the URL as https when `X-Forwarded-Proto` is https). The real fix belongs in H1 (request 99918e60): a configured public origin, or trust in the local proxy's forwarded scheme.\n3. Rate-limit keys behind the proxy. `addressKey` maps every IPv6 link-local address (fe80::/64) to one key, so all link-local clients share one join window; the laptop reaches inguz.local over link-local. The MCP bearer-failure limit keys on the raw address string. Decide the keys for a LAN deployment.\n\nAlso found:\n4. Shutdown order. At a system shutdown launchd stops SeaweedFS and celld together; SeaweedFS's S3 is gone within about 50 ms, celld's handoff fails, and celld runs to its 40 s process deadline. No acknowledged act was lost, but cells are not released. The Mac kit should make the store outlive celld, or celld should skip the handoff as the only node. The persisted system log also stops before the jobs exit, so only each service's own log shows how it stopped.\n5. The session cap (64 per key, packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:385, already item 2 of request a6847815) surfaced in the CLI as \"forbidden\" on a directory read while another client used the same key; it should say rate-limited.\n6. Smaller defects: `dap act set-role --target @m1` crashes with a CanonicalError (NaN target); the first `issueInvitation` returned state unknown and continuing 2 s later gave verified; room creation in the page needs `/v1/demo/creation-offer`, which a self-hosted deployment does not serve.\n\nFor the Mac kit (H3 on macOS) and the documents (G2): the launchd parameters that held (KeepAlive, run as the user, ExitTimeOut 60, ThrottleInterval 70 for celld above its 60 s lease, celld started only after a PUT to the store succeeds); Caddy's `grace_period 10s` (without it a SIGTERM waited 121 s for open streams); the served Caddyfile (Caddyfile.served: one certificate, `header_up CF-Connecting-IP {remote_host}`); the certificate profile that macOS accepts (EC P-256, serverAuth EKU, at most 825 days, SAN names and addresses; 900 days and no EKU are refused); the user trust steps drafted in REPORT.md; and an authenticated restart (`fdesetup authrestart`) for maintenance because FileVault is on. Not tested: Firefox, iOS, and real browser trust instead of bypass flags.","body":{"conditions":"Items 1 to 3 are fixed on main with a witness on celld behind the proxy, or answered by a planner assert naming the celld issue or later slice that owns them; items 4 to 6 are fixed or carried into H1, H3 or G2; the kit and document points are carried into the self-hosting note or G2.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}